<p>Today is the first day of a new reference period. On the basis of exchange rates on 11 April, the UK's RMG is greater than +5 per cent at 5.706. It is therefore, forecast to enter the first of a possible five confirmation periods on 21 April, prior to a possible revaluation on 11 June 1997. All other green rates are currently forecast to remain unchanged. However sterling has strengthened sharply over the past few days. If it maintains this strength next week, it is possible that the 3-day (6 per cent) rule will be triggered by sterling, thus commencing the confirmation period before 21 April and leading to a possible UK green rate revaluation as early as 4 June 1997.</p>
